IMPORT prelude

-- Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (Singapore) -- public agencies (s 25), the liability of network service
-- providers (s 26), and enforcement and offences (ss 16R, 23, 28 to 36, 39, Third Schedule paras 8 and 9).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electronic Transactions Act 2010 -- liability and enforcement`

§§ `25 -- public agencies`

-- s 25(1): a public agency that accepts filings, requires documents, requires originals, issues permits or requires
-- payment "may, despite anything to the contrary in such written law, carry out that function by means of electronic
-- records or in electronic form."
-- s 25(4): "Subject to sections 9 and 10, nothing in this Act by itself compels any public agency to accept or issue
-- any document or information in the form of electronic records or to accept any payment in electronic form."
--
-- "Subject to sections 9 and 10" implies those sections DO compel an agency, where a written law requires retention or
-- an original and the s 9 or 10 conditions (including the agency's own additional requirements) are met. Otherwise an
-- agency may refuse electronic filing.
DECLARE AgencyCase HAS
    `the requirement is one of retention or of an original` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the section 9 or 10 conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS AN AgencyCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agency may refuse the electronic form` IF
    NOT (    `the case`'s `the requirement is one of retention or of an original`
         AND `the case`'s `the section 9 or 10 conditions are met`)

§§ `26 -- network service providers`

-- s 26(1): "a network service provider shall not be subject to any civil or criminal liability under any rule of law
-- in respect of third-party material in the form of electronic records to which the network service provider MERELY
-- PROVIDES ACCESS if such liability is founded on -- (a) the making, publication, dissemination or distribution of such
-- materials or any statement made in such material; or (b) the infringement of any rights subsisting in or in relation
-- to such material."
-- s 26(2): nor any liability under the Personal Data Protection Act 2012 for such material.
-- s 26(3): nothing affects "(a) any obligation founded on contract; (b) the obligation ... under a licensing or other
-- regulatory regime ...; (c) any obligation imposed under any written law or by a court to remove, block or deny access
-- to any material; or (d) any liability ... under the Copyright Act 2021 in respect of a rights infringement".
-- s 26(3A): (1) "does not apply in relation to any liability under section 45E, 45F or 45N of the Broadcasting Act 1994".
-- s 26(4): "provides access" means "the provision of the necessary technical means by which third-party material may be
-- accessed and includes the automatic and temporary storage ... for the purpose of providing access"; "third-party"
-- means "a person over whom the provider has no effective control".
--
-- "NETWORK SERVICE PROVIDER" IS NOT DEFINED. The phrase appears eleven times in the deposited text, and neither s 2 nor
-- s 26(4) defines it. Who is one is taken here as a supplied fact.
--
-- (3A) disapplies only SUBSECTION (1), not (2): a Broadcasting Act online-safety liability is not shielded by (1), and
-- (2) is about the PDPA anyway. (3)(c) means the shield never covers a failure to obey a takedown or blocking direction.
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `defamation or other liability for publishing the material`
    `infringement of rights in the material other than copyright`
    `copyright infringement`
    `the Personal Data Protection Act 2012`
    `breach of contract`
    `breach of a licence condition`
    `failure to obey a direction to remove or block the material`
    `section 45E, 45F or 45N of the Broadcasting Act 1994`

DECLARE NSPCase HAS
    `is a network service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `merely provides access to the material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider has effective control over the person who supplied the material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the basis of liability` IS A Basis

GIVEN `the case` IS AN NSPCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is third-party material to which the provider merely provides access` IF
        `the case`'s `is a network service provider`
    AND `the case`'s `merely provides access to the material`
    AND NOT `the case`'s `the provider has effective control over the person who supplied the material`

GIVEN `the case` IS AN NSPCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 26 shields the provider` IF
        `the material is third-party material to which the provider merely provides access` `the case`
    AND CONSIDER `the case`'s `the basis of liability`
        WHEN `defamation or other liability for publishing the material` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `infringement of rights in the material other than copyright` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Personal Data Protection Act 2012` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act defines network service provider` IF
    FALSE

§§ `Offences and their penalties`

-- The offences, with the maximum fine and term written in each provision, or the general penalty in s 33 ("a fine not
-- exceeding $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both") where "no penalty is expressly
-- provided".
--   s 16R(2): failing to comply with a direction to an ETR system provider -- $50,000, 12 months.
--   s 23(2): failing to comply with a direction to a designated person -- $50,000, 12 months.
--   s 28(3): disclosing information obtained under the Act -- $10,000, 12 months.
--   s 29(3): obstructing access to computers or failing to give technical assistance -- $20,000, 12 months.
--   s 31: obstructing, impeding, ASSAULTING or interfering with the Controller -- no penalty stated, so s 33: $20,000,
--         6 months.
--   Third Schedule para 8: knowingly creating or publishing a certificate for a fraudulent purpose -- $20,000, 2 years.
--   Third Schedule para 9: knowingly misrepresenting identity to a CA -- $10,000, 6 months.
--
-- ASSAULTING THE CONTROLLER CARRIES HALF THE TERM OF NOT HELPING THE CONTROLLER. s 31 obstruction and assault fall to s 33's six
-- months; s 29(3) failure to give "reasonable technical and other assistance" carries twelve. (An assault is also a Penal
-- Code offence, and the Controller is a public servant under s 27(6); this row does not follow the Penal Code.)
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to comply with a direction to an electronic transferable records provider`
    `failing to comply with a direction to a designated person`
    `disclosing information obtained under the Act`
    `obstructing computer access or failing to give technical assistance`
    `obstructing or assaulting the Controller`
    `publishing a certificate for a fraudulent purpose`
    `misrepresenting identity to a certification authority`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a direction to an electronic transferable records provider` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to comply with a direction to a designated person` THEN 50000
    WHEN `disclosing information obtained under the Act` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obstructing computer access or failing to give technical assistance` THEN 20000
    WHEN `obstructing or assaulting the Controller` THEN 20000
    WHEN `publishing a certificate for a fraudulent purpose` THEN 20000
    WHEN `misrepresenting identity to a certification authority` THEN 10000

-- In months.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a direction to an electronic transferable records provider` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to comply with a direction to a designated person` THEN 12
    WHEN `disclosing information obtained under the Act` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing computer access or failing to give technical assistance` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing or assaulting the Controller` THEN 6
    WHEN `publishing a certificate for a fraudulent purpose` THEN 24
    WHEN `misrepresenting identity to a certification authority` THEN 6

§§ `28 -- confidentiality`

-- s 28(1): no disclosure of information obtained under the Act unless (a) with the permission of the person it was
-- obtained from (or the third person whose confidential information it is), (b) for administering or enforcing the Act,
-- (c) to assist a public officer in investigating or prosecuting any offence under any written law, or (d) as required by
-- a court or written law.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `with the permission of the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for administering or enforcing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to assist the investigation or prosecution of an offence under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as required by a court or written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `with the permission of the person concerned`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `for administering or enforcing the Act`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `to assist the investigation or prosecution of an offence under any written law`
    OR  `the disclosure`'s `as required by a court or written law`

§§ `32 -- officers' liability`

-- s 32(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of
-- an officer; or (b) to be attributable to any NEGLECT on the officer's part", the officer is guilty too. "Officer"
-- includes "any person purporting to act in any such capacity". The same for partners and for officers or committee
-- members of an unincorporated association.
GIVEN `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect`

§§ `34 to 36 -- prosecution and composition`

-- s 34: no prosecution "except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor".
-- s 36(1): the Controller may compound a PRESCRIBED compoundable offence for "a sum not exceeding the lower of ...
-- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine ...; (b) $5,000."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can be collected on composition` MEANS
    IF (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) LESS THAN 5000
    THEN `the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE 5000

GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller may compound the offence` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable`

§§ `39 -- transition`

-- s 39(1): the Act applies to acts or transactions in relation to an electronic record "made on or after 1 July 2010".
-- s 39(2): treatment under ss 8, 9 or 15 of the repealed Act immediately before that date is not affected.
-- Dates as yyyymmdd numbers.
GIVEN `the date of the act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2010 Act applies to the act` IF
    `the date of the act` AT LEAST 20100701
